      "reviewedAt": "2026-08-24T11:52:27Z",
      "note": "Reviewed the exploit receipt and call trace, the exact proxy creation trace, verified Proxy and UpgradeGatekeeper source, complete UpgradeComplete event range from proxy deployment through the exploit, implementation storage at both endpoints, pre-exploit artifact hash, pinned VerifierExit source, and Blockaid analysis. The bridge calls proxy 0x961369d347ef7a6896bdd39cbe2b89e3911f521f fifteen times and each call delegates to 0xd12f4d8329584f36aed67f807f42d9a02beb9534, returning true. Factory 0x1787bb09b5958065dd0558012aa1efa662156601 created the proxy in transaction 0x88d1ab73c6f4b447a4411eaf4bbc1f4d8dbd3409fdcf4baef5209b665aa545df and selected that implementation. The proxy permits implementation changes only through master 0x714b2d10210f2a3a7aa614f949259c87613689ab; its verified UpgradeGatekeeper emits UpgradeComplete after applying changes, and no such event exists before exploitation. Blockaid reports a $5 million bridge loss."
